Q: zoom image to the center jquery or javascript A: <p>The problem is it only changing <code>background-size</code> but not setting <code>background-position</code> to <code>center</code>. By default, the background starts from the top-left corner, so when it grows, it expands to the right and bottom.</p>
<p>Here's the fix:</p>
<pre><code>function backgroundAdjust(num, el) {
    var wid = parseInt(num) + parseInt(el.width());
    el.css({
        'background-size': wid + 'px auto',
        'background-position': 'center'
    });
}
</code></pre>
<p>That's it. Adding <code>background-position: center</code> will make the image zoom from the center instead of the top-left corner.</p>

Q: Google Places Autocomplete Widget not appearing when using Angular Material Dialog A: <p>I know this is an ugly fix but it was the only way I could get the drop down to show in an Angular app I recently updated from v14 to v21. Move the pac-container from the &lt;body&gt; to the dialog</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>async initAutoComplete() {
    await google.maps.importLibrary('places');
    const autocomplete = new google.maps.places.Autocomplete(this.addressRef.nativeElement);
    setTimeout(() =&gt; {
      const pacContainer = document.querySelector('.pac-container');
      const dialog = document.querySelector('.mat-mdc-dialog-surface');
      if (pacContainer &amp;&amp; dialog) {
        dialog.appendChild(pacContainer);
      }
    }, 300);

    autocomplete.addListener('place_changed', () =&gt; {
      this.handleAddressChange(autocomplete.getPlace());
    });
  }
</code></pre>
<pre><code>::ng-deep .pac-container {
  position: fixed !important;
}
</code></pre>
